INT. HOCKEY RINK - PLAYERS' BENCH - NIGHT

Cold breath. Steel blades on ice. The crowd's roar leaks from the stands.

TARIQ, twenty-two, a winger, grips his stick, eyes on the ice. DEV, twenty-four, a center, shifts beside him, tapping his skate. COACH EDDIE, sixty, leans over the boards. HAL, fifties, the referee, skates up to the bench.

EDDIE
Tariq, you're up.

TARIQ
Coach, he's been on all night.

EDDIE
Then he's tired. Go.

Dev elbows Tariq.

DEV
Cut left. He always goes right.

TARIQ
You sure?

DEV
He told me once.

HAL
Two minutes, gentlemen.

Tariq vaults the boards. Dev follows. Eddie claps once, hard, and the puck drops.
